f September 26, 2025; and 12 bonus equity shares rejected during the corporate action (with the depositories),  have been credited to a separate demat Suspense Escrow account maintained by the Company on behalf of aforesaid shareholders, in compliance with Regulation 39 of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 and Regulation 294 of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2018.","revisedData":"Revised","revisedDate":null,"revisedRemark":null,"revisedStatus":"Revised","revisionDate":"10-OCT-2025","revisionRemark":"Technical Issue","shareholdingPatternNotes":null,"submissionDate":"08-OCT-2025","symbol":"NAZARA","systemDate":"13-OCT-2025 12:56:43","timeDifference":"00:00:05","typeOfSubmission":null,"underlyingDrs":null,"xbrl":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/xbrl/SHP_1544899_10102025091857_WEB.xml","xbrlFileSize":"499.97 KB"},{"broadcastDate":"21-JUL-2025 22:53:47","cgTimeStamp":null,"countString":null,"date":"30-JUN-2025","desc":"NEW_1","employeeTrusts":"0","format":null,"index":"-","industry":"-","isin":"INE418L01021","name":"Nazara Technologies Limited","newColumn":true,"pr_and_prgrp":"8.31","promoterDematNotes":null,"publicShareholdingNotes":null,"public_val":"91.69","recordId":"201390","remarksWeb":"The Board of Directors of Nazara Technologies Limited (the Company), by way of a resolution passed through circulation on June 16, 2025, approved the allotment of 50,00,000 (Fifty Lakhs) fully paid-up Equity Shares of face value Rs. 4/- (Rupees Four Only) each, at a price of Rs. 990/- (including a premium of Rs. 986/-) per share, on a preferential basis by way of private placement to Axana Estates LLP (the Allottee) for an aggregate consideration of Rs. 4,95,00,00,000/-.  This Preferential Issue triggered an obligation to make an open offer in accordance with Regulation 3(1) and Regulation 4 of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Substantial Acquisition of Shares and Takeovers) Regulations, 2011 (SEBI SAST Regulations).  The open offer, made by Axana Estates LLP (Acquirer 1), Plutus Wealth Management LLP (Acquirer 2) (together referred to as Acquirers) along with Junomoneta Finsol Private Limited being Person Acting in Concert (PAC), concluded on July 07, 2025, i.e, after the closure of reporting quarter ended June 30, 2025.  Following the completion of the open offer, the Allottee (i.e. Acquirer 1), and Acquirer 2 have become promoters of the Company along with existing promoters. Furthermore, PAC, Mr. Arpit Khandelwal, Mr. Mithun Padam Sacheti and Mr. Siddhartha Sacheti being deemed persons acting in concert (Deemed PAC) have been classified under Promoter Group of the Company pursuant to the said open offer.  Therefore, the shareholdings of Acquirers, PAC and Deemed PAC are currently reflected under the Public category in the Shareholding Pattern for the quarter ended June 30, 2025.","revisedData":"N","revisedDate":null,"revisedRemark":null,"revisedStatus":"-","revisionDate":null,"revisionRemark":null,"shareholdingPatternNotes":null,"submissionDate":"21-JUL-2025","symbol":"NAZARA","systemDate":"21-JUL-2025 22:53:51","timeDifference":"00:00:04","typeOfSubmission":null,"underlyingDrs":null,"xbrl":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/xbrl/SHP_1489937_21072025105342_WEB.xml","xbrlFileSize":"272.93 KB"},{"broadcastDate":"25-JUN-2025 10:35:46","cgTimeStamp":null,"countString":null,"date":"16-JUN-2025","desc":"NEW_1","employeeTrusts":"0","format":null,"index":"-","industry":"-","isin":"INE418L01021","name":"Nazara Technologies Limited","newColumn":false,"pr_and_prgrp":"8.31","promoterDematNotes":null,"publicShareholdingNotes":null,"public_val":"91.69","recordId":"199087","remarksWeb":"The Board of Directors of Nazara Technologies Limited (the Company) by way of a resolution passed through circulation on June 16, 2025, has approved the allotment of 50,00,000 (Fifty Lakhs) fully paid-up Equity Shares of face value Rs. 4/- (Rupees Four Only) each, at a price of Rs. 990/- (including premium of Rs. 986/-) per Share, on preferential basis by way of private placement to Axana Estates LLP (the Allottee) for an aggregate consideration of Rs. 4,95,00,00,000/-.  As the aforesaid Preferential Issue has triggered an obligation to make an open offer in terms of Regulation 3(1) and Regulation 4 of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Substantial Acquisition of Shares and Takeovers) Regulations, 2011 (SEBI SAST Regulations), upon completion of the said open offer, the shareholding pattern of the Company will undergo further change.  In terms of Regulation 22(2A) of the SEBI SAST Regulations, the aforesaid Equity Shares allotted to Axana Estates LLP shall not carry any voting rights until the completion of the Open Offer being made by Axana Estates LLP and Plutus Wealth Management LLP (together referred to as the Acquirers), along with Junomoneta Finsol Private Limited as the Person Acting in Concert (PAC), for the acquisition of upto 26% of the Equity Share Capital of the Company, in compliance with the SEBI (SAST) Regulations. Accordingly, these shares will be held in a share escrow account and, upon completion of the Open Offer, shall be transferred to the Allottees demat account. The Equity Shares allotted shall be locked in as per the applicable provisions of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2018.  Upon completion of the aforesaid open offer, the Acquirers shall be classified as promoters and the PAC along with Mr. Arpit Khandelwal, Mr. Mithun Padam Sacheti and Mr. Siddhartha Sacheti (collectively referred to as Deemed PAC) shall be classified as the promoter group along with the existing promoters and promoter group of the Company, in accordance with applicable law. Accordingly, since the open offer process is still ongoing and has not yet been completed, their shareholdings are currently reflected as public shareholdings in the shareholding pattern.","revisedData":"N","revisedDate":null,"revisedRemark":null,"revisedStatus":"-","revisionDate":null,"revisionRemark":null,"shareholdingPatternNotes":null,"submissionDate":"25-JUN-2025","symbol":"NAZARA","systemDate":"25-JUN-2025 10:35:51","timeDifference":"00:00:05","typeOfSubmission":null,"underlyingDrs":null,"xbrl":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/xbrl/SHP_199087_1470673_25062025103545_WEB.xml","xbrlFileSize":null},{"broadcastDate":"18-APR-2025 11:01:22","cgTimeStamp":null,"countString":null,"date":"31-MAR-2025","desc":"NEW_1","employeeTrusts":"0","format":null,"index":"-","industry":"-","isin":"INE418L01021","name":"Nazara Technologies Limited","newColumn":false,"pr_and_prgrp":"8.78","promoterDematNotes":null,"publicShareholdingNotes":null,"public_val":"91.22","recordId":"197891","remarksWeb":"N","revisedData":"N","revisedDate":null,"revisedRemark":null,"revisedStatus":"-","revisionDate":null,"revisionRemark":null,"shareholdingPatternNotes":null,"submissionDate":"18-APR-2025","symbol":"NAZARA","systemDate":"18-APR-2025 11:01:26","timeDifference":"00:00:04","typeOfSubmission":null,"underlyingDrs":null,"xbrl":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/xbrl/SHP_197891_1418075_18042025110121_WEB.xml","xbrlFileSize":null},{"broadcastDate":"25-JAN-2025 13:10:01","cgTimeStamp":null,"countString":null,"date":"17-JAN-2025","desc":"NEW_1","employeeTrusts":"0","format":null,"index":"-","industry":"-","isin":"INE418L01021","name":"Nazara Technologies Limited","newColumn":false,"pr_and_prgrp":"8.79","promoterDematNotes":null,"publicShareholdingNotes":null,"public_val":"91.21","recordId":"196099","remarksWeb":"N","revisedData":"N","revisedDate":null,"revisedRemark":null,"revisedStatus":"-","revisionDate":null,"revisionRemark":null,"shareholdingPatternNotes":null,"submissionDate":"25-JAN-2025","symbol":"NAZARA","systemDate":"25-JAN-2025 13:10:06","timeDifference":"00:00:05","typeOfSubmis